;; The native check's known differences (bin/repr-cpp native-check; doc/cpp/NATIVE.md, "The classes"): a file whose forms read by the
;; native parser differ from the forms read from the oracle's dump, NAME (as the list names it, under its corpus: gxx-dg/, samples/) ->
;; its class. Every class is a fact of clang's Sema the native reader does not compute (CX11: a parser with the names' kinds, no Sema):
;;   :defaulted-noexcept  a defaulted special member's or comparison's exception specification, which clang evaluates when the member is
;;                        used (M m; uses M() = default, which then prints noexcept); unused, it stays unevaluated (no noexcept)
;;   :brace-elision       a braced initializer of an aggregate whose elided braces clang's semantic InitListExpr restores
;;   :ctad                a class template's arguments deduced from an initializer (A a(b); declares an A<int>)
;;   :builtin-signature   a library function's redeclaration with the attributes of clang's builtin or of the header's declaration
;;                        it redeclares (_Nonnull on a parameter, from <stdio.h>'s fprintf)
;;   :clang-recovery      an ill-formed construct clang reads by its error recovery (inline template <int> void foo ())
;; A file the run finds the same that is listed here is an improvement (said, not a failure); one that differs and is not listed fails.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
{"gxx-dg/cpp0x/explicit14.C" :defaulted-noexcept
 "gxx-dg/cpp0x/overload-conv-3.C" :defaulted-noexcept
 "gxx-dg/cpp0x/initlist-value2.C" :defaulted-noexcept
 "gxx-dg/cpp2a/spaceship-union1.C" :defaulted-noexcept
 "gxx-dg/init/array56.C" :defaulted-noexcept
 "gxx-dg/cpp0x/mem-init-aggr1.C" :brace-elision
 "gxx-dg/cpp1z/class-deduction6.C" :ctad
 "gxx-dg/lto/pr45679-1_1.C" :builtin-signature
 "gxx-dg/template/error11.C" :clang-recovery}
